@anon.984efe779a4077b66be6415f964eeb42.2167 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1778 x i8] }> <{ [1778 x i8] c"A bibliography / reference listing.\0A\0AYou can create a new bibliography by calling this function with a path\0Ato a bibliography file in either one of two formats:\0A\0A- A Hayagriva `.yml` file. Hayagriva is a new bibliography file format\0A  designed for use with Typst. Visit its\0A  [documentation](https://github.com/typst/hayagriva/blob/main/docs/file-format.md)\0A  for more details.\0A- A BibLaTeX `.bib` file.\0A\0AAs soon as you add a bibliography somewhere in your document, you can start\0Aciting things with reference syntax (`[@key]`) or explicit calls to the\0A[citation]($cite) function (`[#cite(<key>)]`). The bibliography will only\0Ashow entries for works that were referenced in the document.\0A\0A# Styles\0ATypst offers a wide selection of built-in\0A[citation and bibliography styles]($bibliography.style). Beyond those, you\0Acan add and use custom [CSL](https://citationstyles.org/) (Citation Style\0ALanguage) files. Wondering which style to use? Here are some good defaults\0Abased on what discipline you're working in:\0A\0A| Fields          | Typical Styles                                         |\0A|-----------------|--------------------------------------------------------|\0A| Engineering, IT | `{\22ieee\22}`                                             |\0A| Psychology, Life Sciences | `{\22apa\22}`                                    |\0A| Social sciences | `{\22chicago-author-date\22}`                              |\0A| Humanities      | `{\22mla\22}`, `{\22chicago-notes\22}`, `{\22harvard-cite-them-right\22}` |\0A| Economics       | `{\22harvard-cite-them-right\22}`                          |\0A| Physics         | `{\22american-physics-society\22}`                         |\0A\0A# Example\0A```example\0AThis was already noted by\0Apirates long ago. @arrgh\0A\0AMultiple sources say ...\0A@arrgh @netwok.\0A\0A#bibliography(\22works.bib\22)\0A```" }>, align 1
